a0","fc1f9c34df87358d","fd441caa8d75bfbc","fdd26d6ec947819d","fdd43c2c69479a0f","fe153da25a83aad8","feafb49d5d9438fb","feb666c10477519e","feb98991c3a270a9","ff41c72047c305bd","ff9529da08497753","ffe96ffe7b9a1eef"],"groups":["2b2db5b15314707c","d7c726c1f32e9c8e","bb08665afe2ef87f","196fcce75a4f33af","717220a93f2165f3","a90d57b27de347c5","4b15b5da31baae03","11b7f7740b3eb5b0","5775bbd2865143b0","3c88a0a05e2c7d9f","6bc5ea92c754084e","2732b9235183bf98","4a1a99ec792c0ec0","3de2ed03216f4c4c","77f4de08c4c71d08"],"findings":"The annotations mostly match the code, and I found nothing that needs changing. I ran `node --test test/ary.test.ts` and all 6 tests pass (**verified**). Everything else below is from reading the code (**read**). I did not load the shell in a browser, run the build, or probe the guards myself.\n\n**Mismatches**\n- None. The notes on `ary-server` and `ary-guards` describe what the code does: the Host allowlist, the `-` prefix refusal, `--end-of-options`, and the 200-commit cap. The two-pass `--grep`/`--author` merge and the hand paging are also as described.\n- The 200-character search cap sits in `ary-server`'s `/api/log` route line, as the author says. It is a guard, so `ary-guards` is understated by that one line.\n\n**Misgraded necessity**\n- `ary-ui` is graded **required**, but part of it is polish. The author admits Refresh, Load more, the \"none\" base option and the stale-hash fallback. The in-picker search, debounced commit search and two-line subjects also go beyond \"browse by branch, commit and range\". A minimal shell with selects, a list and a frame would meet the task. Treat roughly the picker combobox and the commit search as supporting or speculative. The UI is about 500 lines with CSS and has no behavioural tests.\n- `ary-guards` is graded **defensive**. The Host check is required for a localhost server that serves source code (DNS rebinding), so it is not optional. The 405 and `limit`/`skip` clamps are the defensive parts. The 200-commit cap is a product choice, as the author says.\n- `reuse-exports` is correctly mechanical. `ary-register`, `ary-build` and `ary-docs` are correctly supporting.\n\n**Removal candidates**\n- Refresh, \"Load more\", the \"none\" base option and the stale-hash fallback in `ary-ui` could be deferred. The cost is small: users reload the page, and the first 100 commits are enough for most branches.\n- Commit search needs the two-pass git workaround in `browse.ts`. Deferring it would simplify `listLog` to a single `git log -n/--skip`. It is a feature the task did not ask for.\n\n**Simplifications**\n- `listLog` pages search results by hand because `--no-walk` is ignored with `-n`. A simpler option is to collect the shas and slice them before the second `git log`, which would avoid slicing text output. It is minor.\n- Several `/api/log` and `/view` failures mean `GlossError`→422 and `BadRequest`→400. This is fine as written.\n\n**Missing risks**\n- Synchronous git per request is listed by the author. `/api/log` with a broad search also runs `git notes list` for two refs and two full `git log` passes on every request, so large repos will feel slow. The same applies to every \"Load more\" click.\n- `--port ''` parses as `Number('') === 0` and silently picks a random port instead of erroring. This is minor.\n- The gloss and review marks come from `git notes list` on each request. With many notes this is O(notes) per call. It is not a correctness problem.\n- The frame is unsandboxed and same-origin with the API, as the author lists. The nonce CSP is the only barrier, and the shell CSP does not restrict `frame-src` beyond `'self'`. This is acceptable for the stated threat model.\n- `refs/remotes/*/HEAD` is filtered by `endsWith('/HEAD')`. A branch literally named `.../HEAD` would also be hidden. This is an edge case only.\n- A branch named `wip` can't be opened by name, which the author already documents.\n\nThe change is reasonably lean except for the picker and search polish inside `ary-ui`. That group is graded required but contains discretionary work.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
