430aa95dfd6c","f77af29e2ae1db28","f77af29e2ae1db28","f7ced1c167e03135","f7dee81d46663c9c","fa9df8b3931cd06f","faa863f143e76133","faea8e39906200dc","fb986fff3ad0ba79","fba89590100e26a0","fbd00a8d56d79d4c","fc1f9c34df87358d","fd441caa8d75bfbc","fd988e8268e90d06","fdd26d6ec947819d","fdd43c2c69479a0f","fe153da25a83aad8","feafb49d5d9438fb","feb666c10477519e","feb98991c3a270a9","ff41c72047c305bd","ffe96ffe7b9a1eef"],"groups":["105a306ec54abd55","bb08665afe2ef87f","f29871c825cfb887","717220a93f2165f3","74132ee3c804c62e","1cb972c80442ce9f","3f2065d26f2785e3","ff8eb382c2ef3e34","60c8fefe7922099e","2732b9235183bf98","3de2ed03216f4c4c","77f4de08c4c71d08"],"findings":"**Review of `git gloss ary`: the annotations mostly hold, with a few grading and coverage gaps.**\n\nI ran `node --test test/ary.test.ts`. All 4 tests pass (**verified**). I did not run the build, the browser shell or the screenshots. The author's headless-Chromium evidence is unchecked.\n\n**Mismatches**\n1. `ary-server` (**read**): the notes say option-looking revisions are refused, but `revParam` only checks a leading `-`. The real protection is `--end-of-options` in `resolveCommits` and `listLog`. `revParam` is a second layer, and `/view?rev=--output=x` returning 400 is tested. The claim is slightly broader than what the check does. It is not a hole.\n2. `ary-server` (**read**): `rev === 'wip'` is special-cased before git is asked, so a real branch named `wip` can never be viewed through the revision box or the sidebar. It is minor and undocumented.\n3. `ary-build` (**read**): the group says it `serves: ary-ui`, but the code that reads the assets is `server.ts` (`ary-server`), so that is the group it serves. Nothing tests `dist/`. The `dist/ary/*` copy and the `node dist` path are unchecked by any test.\n\n**Misgraded necessity**\n- `ary-server` is marked `required` but bundles defensive code. The Host-header check, GET-only, and the 200-commit cap are all defensive or judgment calls. The Host check is warranted, since the page exposes the user's code to DNS rebinding. The cap is a product decision and could be deferred. The API itself would still work without it, and the only cost would be a hung browser on huge ranges.\n- `ary-ui` is `required`, and that fits. Several parts are polish: Refresh, \"Load more\" paging, the `(none)` base option, the stale-hash option fallback, and the dark theme. About 350 lines of client and CSS is more than the task needs.\n- `reuse-exports` and `ary-register` are accurate.\n\n**Removal and deferral candidates**\n- The 500-item and `skip` paging in `/api/log` (and \"Load more\") could be dropped for a first version. The server and its tests carry that logic (`limit`, `skip`, the `more` flag).\n- The `total` count runs an extra `rev-list --count` on every log load. It is only used for the \"Whole branch\" label.\n\n**Missing risks**\n- **Same-origin, unsandboxed frame (read):** `/view` is same-origin with the shell and the API. The author tried `sandbox=allow-scripts` and removed it because it rendered blank. The only barrier against hostile commit text is the nonce CSP and the escaping. A future escaping bug would give a page script access to the API. It is read-only, but it would expose all repo history.\n- **Slow requests block the server (the author's own listed risk):** this also means one slow `/view` stalls the sidebar. Because Host is checked per request, there is no per-request cost beyond git.\n- **Test gaps:** the tests cover neither `/`, `/ary.js` and `/ary.css` serving, nor the `dist/` layout. A broken asset path would pass CI.\n- **Formatting slip (read):** one line in `test/ary.test.ts` is over-indented (the `assert.equal(JSON.parse(...` after the range fetch).\n\nThe change is otherwise lean and the annotations are mostly honest. The fixes worth making are the `ary-build` serves link, a note on the `wip` name shadowing, and a smoke test for the asset routes.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
